vms-fd1: an initialized C++ inline variable is weak on a target with weak
symbols but no COMDAT groups (alpha-dec-vms)

cp_finish_decl calls maybe_commonize_var before the initializer is stored.
For a public inline variable (C++17) with -fweak, maybe_commonize_var ->
comdat_linkage -> make_decl_one_only, and on a target where
SUPPORTS_ONE_ONLY is 0 but weak symbols exist (alpha-dec-vms: EVAX objects
have no COMDAT groups) make_decl_one_only sees DECL_INITIAL == 0 and picks
DECL_COMMON instead of DECL_WEAK.  The initializer is attached afterwards,
so the variable is emitted as an ordinary strong global in every
translation unit that uses it: `constexpr inline int t[] = {1,2,3};` gives
`.globl t`, where the same variable as a template static data member gives
`.weak`.  Two such objects cannot be linked (GCC 14's own tree_code_type in
tree-core.h: %LINK-F-MULDEF linking cc1).  The re-check already done for
!flag_weak is done here too: an initialized vague-linkage variable left
COMMON becomes WEAK.  Targets with COMDAT groups never reach it.

--- a/gcc/cp/decl.cc
+++ b/gcc/cp/decl.cc
@@ -8924,6 +8924,19 @@
 	  if (!flag_weak)
 	    /* Check again now that we have an initializer.  */
 	    maybe_commonize_var (decl);
+	  else if (!SUPPORTS_ONE_ONLY
+		   && DECL_COMDAT (decl) && DECL_COMMON (decl)
+		   && DECL_INITIAL (decl)
+		   && DECL_INITIAL (decl) != error_mark_node)
+	    {
+	      /* maybe_commonize_var ran before the initializer was known, so
+		 on a target with weak symbols but no COMDAT groups
+		 make_decl_one_only chose COMMON.  An initialized variable
+		 cannot be common; make it weak, as it would have been had
+		 the initializer been seen.  */
+	      DECL_COMMON (decl) = 0;
+	      DECL_WEAK (decl) = 1;
+	    }
 	  /* A class-scope constexpr variable with an out-of-class declaration.
 	     C++17 makes them implicitly inline, but still force it out.  */
 	  if (DECL_INLINE_VAR_P (decl)
